<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Mainland Southeast Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Laos</h1><p class="st-meta">1947 CE – 1975 CE · capital Vientiane</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The constitutional monarchy of Laos from 1947 to 1975, independent from 1953 and torn apart by civil war between royalists and the Pathet Lao.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1946 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sisavang-vong">Sisavang Vong</a> agreed to unite <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luang-prabang">Luang Phrabang</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-vientiane">Vientiane</a>, Champasak and other Lao provinces into a single kingdom, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boun-oum">Prince Boun Oum of Champasak</a> renouncing his claims. A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constitution-of-japan">constitution of 1947</a> made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/laos">Laos</a> a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constitutional-monarchy">constitutional monarchy</a> within the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-fourth-republic">French Union</a>, and full independence came in 1953.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The royal capital was <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-luang-phrabang">Luang Prabang</a> and the administrative capital <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-vientiane">Vientiane</a>. Neutralist, rightist and communist factions competed, and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/republic-of-geneva">Geneva</a> conference of 1962 created a coalition under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/souvanna-phouma">Souvanna Phouma</a>. The communist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pathet-lao">Pathet Lao</a>, backed by <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/democratic-republic-of-vietnam">North Vietnam</a>, controlled the east, through which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ho-chi-minh-trail">Ho Chi Minh Trail</a> ran, and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a> waged a massive secret bombing campaign.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> accords of 1973 a new coalition government formed, but in 1975 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pathet-lao">Pathet Lao</a> took power as communist forces won in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/socialist-republic-of-vietnam">Vietnam</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-cambodia-1953-1970">Cambodia</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/savang-vatthana">King Savang Vatthana</a> abdicated on 2 December 1975, and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lao-peoples-democratic-republic">Lao People's Democratic Republic</a> was proclaimed.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-laos.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Laos" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Thommy · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Laos_(1952%E2%80%931975).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1947 CE – 1975 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Vientiane</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Sisavang Vong, Savang Vatthana, Souvanna Phouma</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Theravada Buddhism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Lao</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/laos">Laos</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Royal Lao Government, Laos</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1961&amp;focus=kingdom-of-laos" aria-label="Kingdom of Laos on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7464 1511 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Laos lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7784 1767L7894 1880M7784 1767L7756 1697M7784 1767L5054 728M7784 1767L7784 1767"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7894 1880h0M7756 1697h0M5054 728h0M7784 1767h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7784 1767h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7784 1767h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Vientiane. <a href="/atlas?year=1961&amp;focus=kingdom-of-laos">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
